2025-05-18 20:53:55,047 - agentpress - INFO - response_processor.py:1070 - Tool execution complete: scrape_webpage -> ToolResult(success=True, output='[\n  {\n    "Title": "Cursor (code editor) - Wikipedia",\n    "URL": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cursor_(code_editor)",\n    "Text": "[Jump to content](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cursor_(code_editor)#bodyContent)\\n\\nFrom Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\\n\\nAI-powered integrated development environment\\n\\n|     |     |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| ![](https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/b/b4/Ambox_important.svg/80px-Ambox_important.svg.png) | hide **This article has multiple issues.** Please help **[improve it](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:EditPage/Cursor_(code_editor) \\"Special:EditPage/Cursor (code editor)\\")** or discuss these issues on the **[talk page](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Cursor_(code_editor) \\"Talk:Cursor (code editor)\\")**. _( [Learn how and when to remove these messages](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:Maintenance_template_removal \\"Help:Maintenance template removal\\"))_\\n\\n|     |     |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| [![](https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/9/99/Question_book-new.svg/60px-Question_book-new.svg.png)](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Question_book-new.svg) | This article **relies excessively on [references](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Verifiability \\"Wikipedia:Verifiability\\") to [primary sources](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:No_original_research#Primary,_secondary_and_tertiary_sources \\"Wikipedia:No original research\\")**. Please improve this article by adding [secondary or tertiary sources](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:No_original_research#Primary,_secondary_and_tertiary_sources \\"Wikipedia:No original research\\"). <br>_Find sources:_ [\\"Cursor\\"\\u00a0code editor](https://www.google.com/search?as_eq=wikipedia&q=%22Cursor%22+code+editor)\\u00a0\\u2013\\u00a0[news](https://www.google.com/search?tbm=nws&q=%22Cursor%22+code+editor+-wikipedia&tbs=ar:1) **\\u00b7** [newspapers](https://www.google.com/search?&q=%22Cursor%22+code+editor&tbs=bkt:s&tbm=bks) **\\u00b7** [books](https://www.google.com/search?tbs=bks:1&q=%22Cursor%22+code+editor+-wikipedia) **\\u00b7** [scholar](https://scholar.google.com/scholar?q=%22Cursor%22+code+editor) **\\u00b7** [JSTOR](https://www.jstor.org/action/doBasicSearch?Query=%22Cursor%22+code+editor&acc=on&wc=on)_(February 2025)__([Learn how and when to remove this message](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:Maintenance_template_removal \\"Help:Maintenance template removal\\"))_ |\\n\\n|     |     |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| ![](https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/b/b4/Ambox_important.svg/80px-Ambox_important.svg.png) | This article **contains [promotional content](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:What_Wikipedia_is_not#Wikipedia_is_not_a_soapbox_or_means_of_promotion \\"Wikipedia:What Wikipedia is not\\")**. Please help [improve it](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Cursor_(code_editor)&action=edit) by removing [promotional language](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Spam \\"Wikipedia:Spam\\") and inappropriate [external links](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:External_links#Advertising_and_conflicts_of_interest \\"Wikipedia:External links\\"), and by adding encyclopedic text written from a [neutral point of view](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Neutral_point_of_view \\"Wikipedia:Neutral point of view\\")._(April 2025)__([Learn how and when to remove this message](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:Maintenance_template_removal \\"Help:Maintenance template removal\\"))_ |\\n\\n_([Learn how and when to remove this message](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:Maintenance_template_removal \\"Help:Maintenance template removal\\"))_ |\\n\\n| [![](https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/9c/Cursor_%28code_editor%29.png)](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Cursor_(code_editor).png) |\\n| [Developer(s)](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Programmer \\"Programmer\\") | Anysphere Inc |\\n| Initial release | 2023; 2\\u00a0years ago\\u00a0(2023) |\\n| Written in | [TypeScript](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/TypeScript \\"TypeScript\\") |\\n| [Operating system](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Operating_system \\"Operating system\\") | - [Windows](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Microsoft_Windows \\"Microsoft Windows\\")<br>- [macOS](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MacOS \\"MacOS\\")<br>- [Linux](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Linux \\"Linux\\") |\\n| [Type](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Software_categories#Categorization_approaches \\"Software categories\\") | [Integrated development environment](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Integrated_development_environment \\"Integrated development environment\\") |\\n| [License](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Software_license \\"Software license\\") | Proprietary |\\n| Website | [cursor.com](https://www.cursor.com/) |\\n\\nCursor\\n\\n**Cursor** is a proprietary [AI](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artificial_intelligence \\"Artificial intelligence\\")-powered [integrated development environment](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Integrated_development_environment \\"Integrated development environment\\") for [Windows](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Microsoft_Windows \\"Microsoft Windows\\"), [macOS](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MacOS \\"MacOS\\") and [Linux](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Linux \\"Linux\\") designed to enhance developer productivity by integrating advanced artificial intelligence features directly into the coding environment. It is a fork of [Visual Studio Code](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Visual_Studio_Code \\"Visual Studio Code\\") with additional AI features like code generation, smart rewrites and codebase queries. Cursor is [proprietary software](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Proprietary_software \\"Proprietary software\\") and developed by Anysphere Inc, an applied research lab involved in building AI systems.[\\\\[1\\\\]](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cursor_(code_editor)#cite_note-:0-1) Notably, Cursor\'s agent mode can complete tasks end-to-end, quickly executing commands while keeping programmers in the loop.\\n\\n## Features\\n\\n\\\\[ [edit](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Cursor_(code_editor)&action=edit&section=1 \\"Edit section: Features\\")\\\\]\\n\\nCursor has a wide range of features using [large language models](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Large_language_model \\"Large language model\\") to manipulate text with [autocomplete](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Autocomplete \\"Autocomplete\\") and chat query function. As it is a [fork](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fork_(software_development) \\"Fork (software development)\\") of Visual Studio Code, existing extensions and settings are able to be integrated into the user\'s workflow.[\\\\[1\\\\]](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cursor_(code_editor)#cite_note-:0-1)\\n\\nCursor allows developers to write code using natural language instructions. Users can generate or update parts of their code by providing prompts.[\\\\[1\\\\]](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cursor_(code_editor)#cite_note-:0-1) It can also index the entire codebase, which can be queried in natural language.[\\\\[2\\\\]](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cursor_(code_editor)#cite_note-2) The editor offers smart rewrite capabilities, allowing users to update multiple lines of code simultaneously, which is particularly useful for refactoring and implementing bulk changes efficiently.[\\\\[3\\\\]](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cursor_(code_editor)#cite_note-3) The editor predicts subsequent code edits and user can jump and apply them using tabs.[\\\\[4\\\\]](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cursor_(code_editor)#cite_note-4)\\n\\n## History\\n\\n\\\\[ [edit](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Cursor_(code_editor)&action=edit&section=2 \\"Edit section: History\\")\\\\]\\n\\nAnysphere was founded in 2022 by Sualeh Asif, Arvid Lunnemark, Aman Sanger and Michael Truell, four friends that met while studying at [MIT](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Massachusetts_Institute_of_Technology \\"Massachusetts Institute of Technology\\").[\\\\[5\\\\]](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cursor_(code_editor)#cite_note-techcrunch-5) In 2023, they launched Cursor and later that year raised $8 million in seed funding, led by [OpenAI](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/OpenAI \\"OpenAI\\")\'s Startup Fund.[\\\\[5\\\\]](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cursor_(code_editor)#cite_note-techcrunch-5) In August 2024, Anysphere raised $60 million in a Series A funding round led by [Andreessen Horowitz](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Andreessen_Horowitz \\"Andreessen Horowitz\\"), valuing the company at $400 million.[\\\\[6\\\\]](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cursor_(code_editor)#cite_note-6) In November 2024, Anysphere announced that it had acquired AI coding assistant Supermaven.[\\\\[7\\\\]](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cursor_(code_editor)#cite_note-7) In January 2025, [Thrive Capital](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thrive_Capital \\"Thrive Capital\\") and Andreessen Horowitz led a Series B funding round. Anysphere raised $105 million in this round, which valued the company at $2.5 billion.[\\\\[8\\\\]](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cursor_(code_editor)#cite_note-8)\\n\\nIn April 2025, Cursor experienced a bug impacting the ability to use the software on multiple devices at once. However, a Cursor customer support email using AI-generated responses [hallucinated](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hallucination_(artificial_intelligence) \\"Hallucination (artificial intelligence)\\") a policy prohibiting a single subscription license from being used on multiple devices for security reasons, and incorrectly stated that a separate subscription had to be purchased for each device. Amid criticism of the new \\"policy\\" on [Reddit](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reddit \\"Reddit\\"), an Anysphere spokesperson issued a retraction clarifying that no such policy existed, and that it was an erroneous response from a \\"front-line AI support bot\\".[\\\\[9\\\\]](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cursor_(code_editor)#cite_note-9)\\n\\n## Privacy and security\\n\\n\\\\[ [edit](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Cursor_(code_editor)&action=edit&section=3 \\"Edit section: Privacy and security\\")\\\\]\\n\\nCursor offers privacy options, including a Privacy Mode where the user\'s code is never stored remotely. The platform is SOC 2 certified, ensuring adherence to industry-standard security practices.[\\\\[10\\\\]](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cursor_(code_editor)#cite_note-10)\\n\\n## Community and adoption\\n\\n\\\\[ [edit](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Cursor_(code_editor)&action=edit&section=4 \\"Edit section: Community and adoption\\")\\\\]\\n\\nCursor has garnered attention from engineers at companies such as Shopify, OpenAI, and Instacart.\\\\[ _[citation needed](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Citation_needed \\"Wikipedia:Citation needed\\")_\\\\] Users have reported significant workflow improvements, citing the editor\'s intuitive AI integration and efficiency in code generation and editing.[\\\\[11\\\\]](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cursor_(code_editor)#cite_note-11)\\n\\n## Comparison with other AI code editors\\n\\n\\\\[ [edit](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Cursor_(code_editor)&action=edit&section=5 \\"Edit section: Comparison with other AI code editors\\")\\\\]\\n\\nIn comparison to other AI-powered code editors like [GitHub Copilot](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/GitHub_Copilot \\"GitHub Copilot\\"), Cursor offers deep integration within its standalone environment, providing advanced customization options. While both tools aim to enhance coding efficiency, the choice between them may depend on individual preferences regarding integration and workflow.[\\\\[1\\\\]](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cursor_(code_editor)#cite_note-:0-1)\\n\\n## See also\\n\\n\\\\[ [edit](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Cursor_(code_editor)&action=edit&section=6 \\"Edit section: See also\\")\\\\]\\n\\n- [Visual Studio Code](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Visual_Studio_Code \\"Visual Studio Code\\")\\n- [GitHub Copilot](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/GitHub_Copilot \\"GitHub Copilot\\")\\n- [Vibe coding](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vibe_coding \\"Vibe coding\\")\\n\\n## References\\n\\n\\\\[ [edit](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Cursor_(code_editor)&action=edit&section=7 \\"Edit section: References\\")\\\\]\\n\\n01. ^ [Jump up to: _**a**_](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cursor_(code_editor)#cite_ref-:0_1-0) [_**b**_](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cursor_(code_editor)#cite_ref-:0_1-1) [_**c**_](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cursor_(code_editor)#cite_ref-:0_1-2) [_**d**_](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cursor_(code_editor)#cite_ref-:0_1-3)Aubry, Fran\\u00e7ois (2024-09-02). [\\"Cursor AI: A Guide With 10 Practical Examples\\"](https://www.datacamp.com/tutorial/cursor-ai-code-editor). _DataCamp_. [Archived](https://web.archive.org/web/20241217070248/https://www.datacamp.com/tutorial/cursor-ai-code-editor) from the original on 2024-12-17. Retrieved 2024-12-19.\\n02. **[^](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cursor_(code_editor)#cite_ref-2 \\"Jump up\\")**[\\"Cursor Codebase Understanding\\"](https://www.cursor.com/). _Cursor_. Retrieved 2024-12-20.\\n03. **[^](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cursor_(code_editor)#cite_ref-3 \\"Jump up\\")**[\\"Cursor Smart Rewrites\\"](https://www.cursor.com/). _Cursor_. Retrieved 2024-12-20.\\n04. **[^](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cursor_(code_editor)#cite_ref-4 \\"Jump up\\")**[\\"Cursor AI Autocompletion\\"](https://www.cursor.com/). _Cursor_. [Archived](https://web.archive.org/web/20241219225622/https://www.cursor.com/) from the original on 2024-12-19. Retrieved 2024-12-20.\\n05. ^ [Jump up to: _**a**_](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cursor_(code_editor)#cite_ref-techcrunch_5-0) [_**b**_](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cursor_(cod